# Merged-tree gate for `tools/tasks close`: one command per line, run in a throwaway worktree that
# holds main + the task branch. Any non-zero exit refuses the close and moves nothing.
# Read from the MAIN checkout only, so a task branch cannot relax the gate that judges it.
# A relative tool path the fresh worktree lacks (.venv/bin/..., node_modules/.bin/...) runs from main.
# Put the project's real lint + test commands here. Empty = no gate, and close prints a warning.
#
# Examples:
#   .venv/bin/ruff check src tests
#   .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q
#   npm run -s typecheck
#   npm test --silent
#   bash -n bin/mytool
